\begin_layout Standard
For each row below, use an active-set guess and the KKT system from Question 1 to find 
\begin_inset Formula $(c^*,n^*,H^*)$
\end_inset

, report 
\begin_inset Formula $q^*=H^*/n^*$
\end_inset

 when defined, identify the active inequalities, and give one valid vector 
\begin_inset Formula $(\eta,\alpha,\beta)$
\end_inset

. Also report the marginal value of income 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda=1+\eta$
\end_inset

. The snapshots vary income and relative costs jointly; they are not a ceteris-paribus claim that income alone determines fertility.
